divergence_reason = sanctioned: this program uses Db.open + Db.withTransaction + Db.exec (SqlValue params) + Db.deleteWhere (backlog #61 — the SqlFragment-typed row-count deletion counterpart to Db.findWhere) — the Go backend and ipê share the Sky stdlib surface but the Go reference emits Go+SQLite binaries while ipê emits Rust+sqlx; the SQLite in-memory behaviour and row-type representation differ enough that a shared Main.ipe cannot run on both backends. ipê's output is recorded as the correct reference. `Db.deleteWhere` itself has no Go counterpart (it is an ipê-only addition), so this divergence is structural, not incidental.
